===============================================================
 Ordinary main checkouts reached through a gitdir link
 previous commit e1dd6d4 vs target commit d2ee9e8
 git 2.43.0, node v24.18.1
===============================================================

=== A. git init --separate-git-dir (named in the goal description) ===

$ cat separate/.git
  gitdir: /tmp/stepstone-r3/gitdir/elsewhere.git
$ git -C separate rev-parse --absolute-git-dir; ... --git-common-dir; ... --show-toplevel
  /tmp/stepstone-r3/gitdir/elsewhere.git
  /tmp/stepstone-r3/gitdir/elsewhere.git
  /tmp/stepstone-r3/gitdir/separate
  ^ git-dir equals git-common-dir, so this checkout IS the main worktree.
$ git -C separate worktree list --porcelain | head -1
  worktree /tmp/stepstone-r3/gitdir/elsewhere.git
  ^ but the listing names the Git directory, not the checkout.

previous commit e1dd6d4 $ stepstone project add "Plan the next release"
Project worklist /tmp/stepstone-r3/gitdir/separate/.worklist/worklist.json cannot be changed from /tmp/stepstone-r3/gitdir/separate: the repository at /tmp/stepstone-r3/gitdir/elsewhere.git has no main worktree, so no checkout of it is the roadmap's sole writer. Restore the main worktree if it was removed, or make this change in a clone that has one; a store outside the committed roadmap paths, named by $STEPSTONE_WORKLIST, stays writable here.
[exit 1]

target commit           $ stepstone project add "Plan the next release"
Added project goal plan-the-next-release: Plan the next release
[exit 0]

roadmap in the separate-git-dir checkout:
  - plan-the-next-release

--- and a worktree added beside it is still refused ---

$ git -C separate worktree add ../separate-agent -b feature/agent
  Preparing worktree (new branch 'feature/agent')
  HEAD is now at 6a59c35 roadmap

target commit           $ stepstone project add "Would fork from a linked worktree"
Project worklist /tmp/stepstone-r3/gitdir/separate-agent/.worklist/worklist.json cannot be changed from /tmp/stepstone-r3/gitdir/separate-agent: the repository at /tmp/stepstone-r3/gitdir/elsewhere.git has no main worktree, so no checkout of it is the roadmap's sole writer. Restore the main worktree if it was removed, or make this change in a clone that has one; a store outside the committed roadmap paths, named by $STEPSTONE_WORKLIST, stays writable here.
[exit 1]

$ git -C separate-agent status --short
  (clean - the linked worktree changed nothing)

=== B. a Git submodule working tree ===

$ cat parent/sub/.git
  gitdir: ../.git/modules/sub
$ git -C parent/sub rev-parse --absolute-git-dir; ... --git-common-dir; ... --show-toplevel
  /tmp/stepstone-r3/gitdir/parent/.git/modules/sub
  /tmp/stepstone-r3/gitdir/parent/.git/modules/sub
  /tmp/stepstone-r3/gitdir/parent/sub
  ^ the submodule is the only worktree of its own repository.
$ git -C parent/sub worktree list --porcelain | head -1
  worktree /tmp/stepstone-r3/gitdir/parent/.git/modules/sub

previous commit e1dd6d4 $ stepstone project add "Track the submodule work"
Project worklist /tmp/stepstone-r3/gitdir/parent/sub/.worklist/worklist.json cannot be changed from /tmp/stepstone-r3/gitdir/parent/sub: the repository at /tmp/stepstone-r3/gitdir/parent/.git/modules/sub has no main worktree, so no checkout of it is the roadmap's sole writer. Restore the main worktree if it was removed, or make this change in a clone that has one; a store outside the committed roadmap paths, named by $STEPSTONE_WORKLIST, stays writable here.
[exit 1]

target commit           $ stepstone project add "Track the submodule work"
Added project goal track-the-submodule-work: Track the submodule work
[exit 0]

roadmap in the submodule working tree:
  - track-the-submodule-work
